# RFC-0016 K9e: the pin suites the pin-strength measurement runs against each
# mutant of the walker's arithmetic and raise arms (scripts/pin-strength.sh;
# docs/rfc-data/0016-k9e.md). In order: the runner stops at the first suite
# that fails, so the broadest killers come first. Each is registered, green on
# its base, and pins its verdicts natively (pinFind / pinExact / pinCrash).
# Changing the list changes what the figure measures: rerun the measurement
# and recommit tests/0016-pinstrength.tsv with it.

# + - * div mod as compound operands of an assertion, int and its widths
tsymex_phase15_A1_arithmetic
# signed add/sub/mul OverflowDefect at each width, checks on
tsymex_phase16_R16_4_overflow
# div/mod DivByZeroDefect, signed and unsigned
tsymex_phase16_R16_3_divzero
# int8..int64 / uint widening conversions, signed vs unsigned compare
tsymex_r6_b2_intwidth
# RangeDefect on a range assignment and conversion
tsymex_phase16_R16_2_rangedefect
# low(T) div/mod -1 at 32 and 64 bits
tsymex_0016_w1d1a_intminmod
# unsigned div/mod by zero
tsymex_0016_w1d1b_udivzero
# a width-typed svInt keeps its OverflowDefect fork
tsymex_r6_r3_svint_overflow
# checks off: wrap, and the C traps of div/mod
tsymex_rfc0005_s8aa_remainder_checksoff
# a range subtype's base width (int32 range) bounds its arithmetic
tsymex_162_range_base_width
# a promoted value keeps its overflow obligation (the discharge log)
tsymex_161_overflow_obligation
# K9e kill pins: Int-sorted compare/arith, width bounds, unsigned wrap, BV compare (cmp cluster)
tsymex_0016_k9e_kill_cmp
# K9e kill pins, -fwrapv build: signed wrap and 8-bit div wrap of an Int-sorted value
tsymex_0016_k9e_kill_cmp_fwrapv
